olored \"saddle\" on the lower part of its back.","revisionId":1356979074,"title":"Milne-Edwards's sifaka","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milne-Edwards%27s_sifaka","wikidataId":"Q1202844"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Indri","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Indri Lemur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Babakoto","source":"Indriidae"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Indri indri","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Indri indri (Gmelin, 1788)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2436432},"ottId":696022,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Indri indri","synonyms":["Indri brevicaudatus","Indri indri indri","Indri indri variegatus","Indri niger","Indris ater","Indris brevicaudatus","Indris variegatus","Lemur indri"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The indri ( ; Indri indri), also called the babakoto, is one of the largest living lemurs, with a head-body length of about 64–72 cm (25–28+1⁄2 in) and a weight of between 6 and 9.5 kg (13 and 21 lb). It has a black and white coat and maintains an upright posture when climbing or clinging.","revisionId":1376950353,"title":"Indri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indri","wikidataId":"Q203868"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Large Shearwaters","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"},{"language":"en","name":"Shearwater","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Calonectris","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Calonectris Mathews & Iredale, 1915","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2481517},"ottId":944662,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Calonectris","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Calonectris is a genus of seabirds. The genus name comes from Ancient Greek kalos, \"good\" and nectris, \"swimmer\".","revisionId":1334916527,"title":"Calonectris","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calonectris","wikidataId":"Q1049267"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Axolotl","source":"The IUCN R